    "blogtextliquid_LBJgtB": {
      "type": "blogtextliquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>Walk into Sephora on a Saturday afternoon and an impeccably dressed sales associate will happily spray you with a 50ml bottle that retails for $320. The bottle is heavy, the cap snaps shut with a reassuring magnetic click, and the display is bathed in immaculate spotlighting.</p><p>You walk away smelling fantastic, but also wondering: how on earth does scented alcohol cost $320? Where does all that money actually go? The answer is a case study in modern luxury marketing, and it explains why the traditional perfume retail model is ripe for disruption.</p>"
      }
    },
