    "blogtextliquid_ra7Awx": {
      "type": "blogtextliquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>In a standard $300 designer perfume bottle, the actual fragrance oil—the compound that creates the scent on your skin—typically costs between $3 and $6 to produce. That is not a typo. The raw ingredients account for roughly 1.5% to 2% of the retail price tag.</p><p>The remaining 98% of your purchase price is consumed by a massive chain of markups, licensing royalties, advertising budgets, and retail real estate. Here is the exact line-by-line financial breakdown.</p>"
      }
    },
    "blocks_ji7beH": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "blog_editorial_text_section_zNd6WG": {
          "type": "blog--editorial-text-section",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Marketing & Packaging Overhead vs Formula Investment",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "heading_size_mobile": 28,
            "heading_line_height": 1.1,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_margin_bottom": 30,
            "heading_margin_bottom_mobile": 25,
            "column_1_text": "<p>Traditional designer perfume brands operate like entertainment studios. They spend tens of millions securing Hollywood A-listers for advertising campaigns, buying prime billboard space in Times Square, and taking out double-page spreads in fashion magazines.</p><p>On top of that, bespoke bottle glass molds, zinc alloy caps, and ornate retail display cases add another $30 to $50 per unit before the retailer takes their mandatory 50% markup.</p>",
            "column_2_text": "<p>At Scentspired, we strip away every penny of that vanity overhead. We do not hire celebrities, we do not pay millions for department store shelf placement, and we use clean, minimalist, standardized glass bottles.</p><p>Every dollar saved is redirected into sourcing the finest French fragrance oils and formulating at rich 20-25% concentrations, delivering exceptional scent performance directly to your doorstep for $45.</p>",
            "body_size": 17,
            "body_size_mobile": 15,
            "body_line_height": 1.9,
            "body_color": "#2D2A26",
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "column_gap": 55,
            "column_gap_mobile": 30,
            "max_width": 1100,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "background_color": "#FAF8F5",
            "padding_top": 60,
            "padding_bottom": 60,
            "padding_horizontal": 40,
            "padding_top_mobile": 40,
            "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
            "padding_horizontal_mobile": 20
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "blog_editorial_text_section_zNd6WG"
      ],
      "name": "Editorial text section",
      "settings": {}
    },
    "1778690749e24fd023": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "blog_narrative_content_9nTtAA": {
          "type": "blog--narrative-content",
          "settings": {
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "max_width": 1100,
            "section_padding": 60,
            "background_color": "#FAF8F5",
            "heading": "<p>Where an inspired perfume spends that same money instead</p>",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_spacing": 25,
            "box_color": "#1C1917",
            "box_radius": 15,
            "box_padding": 45,
            "box_spacing": 35,
            "box_paragraph_1": "<p>A common suspicion is: if an inspired perfume costs $45, does that mean the ingredients are cheap? Absolutely not. Because our overhead is a tiny fraction of a designer house, we actually spend a higher percentage of our manufacturing budget on the fragrance essence itself than many $300 brands.</p><p>We source certified perfume oils formulated in Grasse, France—the historic perfume capital of the world—utilizing the identical molecular building blocks found in the originals.</p><p>When you spray <strong>Addiction</strong> or <strong>Fierce</strong>, you are experiencing high-grade perfumery without paying for a corporation's global marketing apparatus.</p>",
            "box_paragraph_2": "",
            "box_paragraph_3": "",
            "box_text_color": "#F5EFE6",
            "box_text_size": 17,
            "box_text_line_height": 1.9,
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "subheading": "<p>Does a smaller marketing budget mean a lesser scent?</p>",
            "subheading_size": 42,
            "subheading_color": "#1A1816",
            "subheading_spacing": 40,
            "bottom_text": "<p>Olfactory molecules do not care who is featured in the television commercial. Bergamot smells like bergamot; natural cedarwood radiates like cedarwood. Your skin reacts to the chemical purity and concentration of the oils, not the prestige of the logo on the box.</p><p>When you remove the branding, true luxury is how you feel when you wear it every day.</p>",
            "bottom_text_size": 17,
            "bottom_text_color": "#2D2A26",
            "bottom_text_line_height": 1.9
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "blog_narrative_content_9nTtAA"
      ],
      "settings": {}
    },
