        "blog_editorial_callout_section_m8PFU4": {
          "type": "blog--editorial-callout-section",
          "settings": {
            "container_width": 1100,
            "left_column_width": 45,
            "right_column_width": 55,
            "column_gap": 50,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "heading": "What this means when you are shopping",
            "heading_font": "serif",
            "heading_size": 42,
            "mobile_heading_size": 28,
            "heading_color": "#1A1816",
            "heading_indent": 0,
            "mobile_heading_indent": 0,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/WhatsApp_Image_2026-07-03_at_9.01.41_AM.jpg",
            "image_max_width": 500,
            "heading_image_gap": 16,
            "mobile_heading_image_gap": 20,
            "body_text": "<p>The next time you are tempted by a $300 price tag at a department store counter, ask yourself what you are actually buying. Are you paying for the liquid in the bottle, or are you financing an international advertising campaign?</p><p>Try our inspired fragrances side-by-side with your favorite designer scents. You'll get the identical luxury scent experience with enough savings left over to build a versatile 4-bottle wardrobe.</p>",
            "body_font": "system_ui_n4",
